CORE
main.c
--32 --unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por --array-rf-bytes --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
Reading a[i].f while another thread stores a[i].g is no data race. The load at a symbolic element read every member of each element; the member is now selected before the element, so only the f leaves are read. Fails on a binary without the fix.
